                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "120e1377-b40a-4d41-b94c-e9df985df55d",
                        "source_entry_id": "3f4c0d98-d9ef-3711-b9a7-b87b81ef72f1",
                        "source_sense_id": "9e3ce87c-18f9-362a-9a04-cac821da1741",
                        "target_lang_word": "diaphan",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "diaphan",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "40d3c31b-143d-380b-ab56-7517a8168652",
                                        "entry_id": "01673617-a855-308b-871b-0dc408a3cef4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "so beschaffen, dass etwas von Licht durchdrungen werden kann"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a067a846-d89b-4d64-a3eb-c5e616c1610f",
                                                "sense_id": "40d3c31b-143d-380b-ab56-7517a8168652",
                                                "text": "Das Exponat war mit einer diaphanen Folie zugedeckt, um es vor schädlichen Einflüssen zu schützen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea9b9ce0-6ca7-4673-a799-5eb26c5a1c51",
                                                "sense_id": "40d3c31b-143d-380b-ab56-7517a8168652",
                                                "text": "„Dunstleer und diaphan ist die Atmosphäre nur da, wo wir die dunkeln Streifen erblicken.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d0e45fd7-273a-4468-bbdb-e1d0a5e135c8",
                        "source_entry_id": "3f4c0d98-d9ef-3711-b9a7-b87b81ef72f1",
                        "source_sense_id": "9e3ce87c-18f9-362a-9a04-cac821da1741",
                        "target_lang_word": "diaphane",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "diaphane",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d12a23f1-24d0-3a1c-8765-15369d35c5b6",
                                        "entry_id": "5f97990d-3c50-3813-98f9-458626249877",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something transparent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4533e995-0e75-4f41-a979-72e695d0defe",
                                                "sense_id": "d12a23f1-24d0-3a1c-8765-15369d35c5b6",
                                                "text": "The corporal nature is deuided into bright and ſhining bodies, as earth and metalles: Eyther into Diaphane or tranſparent bodyes, as ayre and water."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd377e69-f344-4166-952f-6a44c6e9b5df",
                                                "sense_id": "d12a23f1-24d0-3a1c-8765-15369d35c5b6",
                                                "text": "And for man's life as the clear sparkling wine, Gladding the heart and lifting up the soul From its frail diaphane of petulant flesh, Yet whence doth flow this liquor of delight?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b649264-a8e0-461e-bd16-51a5279232a0",
                                                "sense_id": "d12a23f1-24d0-3a1c-8765-15369d35c5b6",
                                                "text": "Here, dragonflies of metallic emerald-gold or ruby iridescence froze in midair on almost-invisible wings of diaphane."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a65d3d0-c717-49f4-a710-f4666e0059eb",
                                                "sense_id": "d12a23f1-24d0-3a1c-8765-15369d35c5b6",
                                                "text": "I moulded with my hands The mobile breasts, the valley; and the waist I touched; and pigments reverently placed Upon their thighs in sapient spots and stains, Beryls and crysolites and diaphanes, And gems whose hot harsh names are never said."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af3137d5-ca7f-3454-b127-745dbaf39cc8",
                                        "entry_id": "5f97990d-3c50-3813-98f9-458626249877",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A woven silk stuff with transparent and colored figures."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc1c7e9e-4e8f-35c1-a13b-835210411a48",
                                        "entry_id": "5f97990d-3c50-3813-98f9-458626249877",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Essence or nature as encapsulated in a mental construct."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7ad89ce-a23d-48cf-ac03-028f7076300a",
                                                "sense_id": "bc1c7e9e-4e8f-35c1-a13b-835210411a48",
                                                "text": "The figure of the diaphane, \"this clear crystal nature,\" is a person so perfect that his simple presence would do more for the world than others manage to do through their actions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c947203-5cd2-41c3-bc20-93f7c34629f8",
                                                "sense_id": "bc1c7e9e-4e8f-35c1-a13b-835210411a48",
                                                "text": "Thus dreams and daydreams, stray thoughts, and all the other products of imagination are not simply inside one human brain; some are created by the diaphane of the person who experiences them, others come form outside, but all are projected onto the astral light."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4145bac-bb94-45cc-8fb4-066289cee957",
                                                "sense_id": "bc1c7e9e-4e8f-35c1-a13b-835210411a48",
                                                "text": "What becomes a topic of conversation, what becomes the subject of publicly circulating discourses, is what lies beyond the senses — the land above the sky, the world of the dead, the other side of the diaphane."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f04e48bd-f41f-4a2c-a075-7a91f449ed9e",
                        "source_entry_id": "3f4c0d98-d9ef-3711-b9a7-b87b81ef72f1",
                        "source_sense_id": "9e3ce87c-18f9-362a-9a04-cac821da1741",
                        "target_lang_word": "diaphane",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "diaphane",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3c98a609-7ea7-3bd9-8bbe-8bc7b7a4759f",
                                        "entry_id": "3d0616ed-5429-37fc-aaa9-81508a7b2e8b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui laisse passer à travers soi les rayons lumineux."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5720d060-0c03-4135-b37a-a94418d2bb83",
                                                "sense_id": "3c98a609-7ea7-3bd9-8bbe-8bc7b7a4759f",
                                                "text": "L’air est plus diaphane que l’eau."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "42e6f130-2fa6-33dc-9997-cc73b08f82db",
                                        "entry_id": "3d0616ed-5429-37fc-aaa9-81508a7b2e8b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui laisse passer la lumière sans que les objets soient discernables."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "763f848b-1900-42b5-94c2-847de9c94c1c",
                                                "sense_id": "42e6f130-2fa6-33dc-9997-cc73b08f82db",
                                                "text": "Aucune falaise, […], n’aurait pu donner une idée de cette banquise, opaque en un endroit, diaphane en un autre, et sur laquelle la lumière et l’ombre produisaient les jeux les plus étonnants."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e252dd8-3fd1-3081-9c4b-d855fc691dea",
                                        "entry_id": "3d0616ed-5429-37fc-aaa9-81508a7b2e8b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Transparent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal",
                                            "hyperbole"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53806815-53ca-44eb-b88c-20c567e170bd",
                                                "sense_id": "9e252dd8-3fd1-3081-9c4b-d855fc691dea",
                                                "text": "Ce sont les larves des pucerons […]. Complètement développées, ces larves deviennent de jolis insectes, pourvus de quatre ailes diaphanes, presque deux fois plus longues et plus larges que le corps entier, et soutenues par quelques rares nervures."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e79d25b-cf9a-474f-bef3-d1d24315d55a",
                                                "sense_id": "9e252dd8-3fd1-3081-9c4b-d855fc691dea",
                                                "text": "Dès l’aube quand, au loin, le Djebel Aurès s’irisait de lueurs diaphanes, Yasmina sortait de son humble gourbi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de271844-ee82-4a6d-b385-044d4d9d6c7b",
                                                "sense_id": "9e252dd8-3fd1-3081-9c4b-d855fc691dea",
                                                "text": "Le vent, en un mot, était, en termes de potentialités, aussi riche que la littérature ou la musique, à cette différence qu’on n’en connaissait pas à ce jour le compositeur — ce génie brut et diaphane, qui inventait ses symphonies à la frontière de l’assimilable et nous laissait chancelants, sous le déluge de sa dictée, avec nos vingt et un pauvres signes standard, le blanc pour toute mesure du temps et nos cerveaux à la remorque."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a68535d2-542a-3eb4-ad2d-10f54f15adaa",
                                        "entry_id": "3d0616ed-5429-37fc-aaa9-81508a7b2e8b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "D’apparence fragile et délicat en parlant du physique d'une personne."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd5b191c-5959-464c-b921-25461aba81d0",
                                                "sense_id": "a68535d2-542a-3eb4-ad2d-10f54f15adaa",
                                                "text": "Jacques … constatait combien ces mains, longues, maigres et décharnées, étaient blanches, diaphanes, … il remarquait également leur forme élégante, leur extrême distinction, et la finesse du poignet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce3ae72a-9574-4999-a401-df21536b17f2",
                                                "sense_id": "a68535d2-542a-3eb4-ad2d-10f54f15adaa",
                                                "text": "J’éprouvais une curiosité terrifiée pour ce nouvel aspect de la femme.\nPendant tant de siècles, comment avions-nous pu croire qu’elle était cette créature diaphane qui s’évanouissait ? Cet être aux yeux de biche dont la taille tenait dans un anneau de rideau."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "685589a1-b8d1-4655-818b-fe1a9a9c3f8b",
                        "source_entry_id": "3f4c0d98-d9ef-3711-b9a7-b87b81ef72f1",
                        "source_sense_id": "9e3ce87c-18f9-362a-9a04-cac821da1741",
